{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481513-monks-perfected-adepts-2e-conversion","id":1481513,"title":"Monks (Perfected Adepts 2e conversion)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-19T20:49:33-07:00","id":1481513,"title":"Monks (Perfected Adepts 2e conversion)","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perfected Adept</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Monks</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pages 349-351 of Mage the Awakening First edition for lore*</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Doctrine and Magic</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Path:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Obrimos </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Parent Order:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Adamantine Arrow</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span></b> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 2, Forces 1, 2 dots in Brawl, one of the following additional skills at 2 dots or higher: Athletics, Medicine, Intimidation, Survival, Streetwise</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Initiation:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The initiate spends a full day cycling between martial arts training, sparing, and meditating on the teachings of the legacy</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling Arcana:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Life</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yantras:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Casting in a place of physical training, such as a gym, dojo, or running track (+1); swearing an oath of service or performing another genuine act of humility (+1); fasting for at least a day (+2); discarding something of value or a vanity (+1-3 depending on significance).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Oblations:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Drilling or training in combat techniques, including katas, sword forms, sparring, punching bag work, etc.; feats of endurance, such as running a marathon or long exposure to the elements; successfully meditating (Mage, p. 208) for at least an hour.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Attainments</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>First Attainment: Body Temple </b></span></span>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With an hour of focused meditation, Perfected Adepts are able to enhance their senses. This is the first step in truly mastering the body. This attainment functions as \u201c</span></span>Heightened Senses<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201d (Life 1, MtAw 148) targeting the monk, with reach for advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Forces 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The meditation does not only need to apply to the health of the body. Those initiates in Forces can learn how to focus on the energy that flows through their bodies, enhancing the body's use of that energy. This attainment functions as \u201cKinetic Efficiency\u201d (Forces 1, MtAw 141) targeting the monk, with reach for advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Second Attainment: Chi Force</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Life 2, 3 dots in Brawl</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Meditations now give the monks enhanced control of their own body, allowing them to control and enhance its natural functions. This attainment functions as \u201cBody Control\u201d (Life 2, MtAw 148) targeting the monk, with reach for advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Forces 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Greater control over the body can lead some monks to greater control over the kinetic energy that flows through their body, allowing them to strike with more lethal attacks. This attainment functions as \u201cKinetic Blow\u201d (Forces 2, MtAw 143)targeting the monk, with reach for advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Third Attainment: Perfect Body</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 3, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 3 or a second option from the list must be raised to 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Monks who have reached this level of mastery over their own bodies are able to push their body past its limits through their meditations, removing their physical weaknesses. This attainment functions as \u201cHoning the Form\u201d (Life 3, MtAw 150) targeting the monk, with reach for advanced duration.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Forces 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this point of their training the monks can now release the kinetic force of their body through the air. With this Attainment the Adept can strike their foes from a distance. They can treat their Brawl attacks as though they had range increments of Forces dots/2x Forces dots/4x Forces dots. The Kinetic Blows effect of the optional second attainment can be applied to these attacks. If the Perfected Adept has the Fast Spells merit then the attacks are treated as firearms attacks for the purposes of the target's Defense. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fourth Attainment: Restoring Form</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Life 4, 4 dots in Brawl</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bruises heal and broken bones snap back into place at the will of the monk. This attainment works as \u201cKnit\u201d (Life 3, MtAw 150) targeting the monk, with reach for instant casting and to allow the mage to heal personal tilts such as arm wrack. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Forces 4</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Perfected Adept can unleash an astonishing flurry of blows. The Perfected Adept treats all their Brawl attacks as having the Medium Burst property (MtAw 219).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Fifth Attainment: Mastery of the Self</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Life 5, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 5, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 4 or a second option from the list must be raised to 3 or a third option must be raised to 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Monk\u2019s mastery over their own body allows them to increase the speed at which their body heals. It only takes them a moment of focus to heal wounds they suffer in combat. This attainment functions as \u201cMend\u201d (Life 4, MtAw 152) targeting the monk, with reach for instant casting. Additionally, by spending a mana they can heal aggravated damage instead of lethal. The mage as such control over their body that they can heal any wound. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Optional: Forces 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The monk can channel the kinetic energy of their body into a destructive force on the world around them, destroying buildings around them. This attainment functions as \u201cEarthquake\u201d (Forces 5, MtAw 147) with reach for instant casting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">*</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Perfected Adepts also have a small write up in \u201cNameless and Accursed\u201d p. 26.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 04-02-2023, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T20:50:32-07:00","id":1481514,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, this is my first legacy conversion, appreciate all the help I got in private over discord on it. Felt very anime when I read over the older version of it so I leaned into that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T11:43:14-07:00","id":1481544,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the situations that the first Attainment would help with, but Heightened Senses with Reach assigned to advanced duration seems more versatile. It would allow them to sense any sources of poison and detect ambushes. Cleanse the Body would be less useful in combat. Since Purge Illness can be consistently used with Life 2 to solve the problem entirely, it diminishes the aid Cleanse the Body provides.<br /> <br /> I think it could be interesting to move Kinetic Blow to the third optional Attainment, since being able to use the extra Reach to have an equivalent of Stunning Strike sounds pretty fun. In its place, you could use a spell inspired by Control Gravity. This allows the subject to walk on walls or ceilings. Reach would be assigned to advanced duration and you could activate in the same interval as Kinetic Efficiency. With that, you cover most acrobatics short of platforming on leaves and raindrops.<br /> <br /> The fourth Life Attainment could be a variation of Shrink and Grow, allowing the mage to alter the size of any living being. Reach could be assigned to instant use and advanced duration. This allows them to have an even easier time staying close to enemies, gives them some extra Health (since Size affects that) and makes them far more difficult to target with spells. A master of Life would have a size of 5 (base) + 5 (Potency) + 2 (Legacy extra factor dice) = 12. This means all enemies need at least that to affect them or take extra time using something like Warding Gesture (which not everyone will have) or cast with AoE factors, which risks putting themselves and their allies in the crossfire. This way you avoid a functionality overlap between Mend and Knit, while also gaining an ability that is useful both in and out of combat (shrinking has a lot of creative stealth applications).<br /> <br /> The fourth optional Attainment is based on Flurry of Blows, correct ? In that case, utilizing a spell as a basis, I would say this is similar to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1053502#post1053502\">Gatling Assault</a>, with Reach used for instant use and medium burst autofire. It takes a turn to setup and van be used [Forces] times, but makes it unblockable if you can't defend against firearms.<br /> <br /> The capstone Attainment can be used on both the monk or anyone they touch, by default spell rules.<br /> <br /> The last optional Attainment of Earthquake might be a bit too wide hitting for the self displine approach of the Legacy. An alternative could be to use Turn Momentum with Reach assigned to advanced duration, reflexive use and redirecting objects up to 90 degrees. This allows them to protect themselves plus cabalmates and control some of the chaos around them to their favor.<br /> <br /> Those would be my first thoughts on this conversion, the idea was to synergize the toolkit to create a highly mobile and versatile close range brawler. Hope it helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-20-2022, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-20T15:05:44-07:00","id":1481559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481513-monks-perfected-adepts-2e-conversion?p=1481544#post1481544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about the situations that the first Attainment would help with, but Heightened Senses with Reach assigned to advanced duration seems more versatile. It would allow them to sense any sources of poison and detect ambushes. Cleanse the Body would be less useful in combat. Since Purge Illness can be consistently used with Life 2 to solve the problem entirely, it diminishes the aid Cleanse the Body provides.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah after looking over this I agree, it is much more useful and still fits within the theme for the legacy, good change here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481513-monks-perfected-adepts-2e-conversion?p=1481544#post1481544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it could be interesting to move Kinetic Blow to the third optional Attainment, since being able to use the extra Reach to have an equivalent of Stunning Strike sounds pretty fun. In its place, you could use a spell inspired by Control Gravity. This allows the subject to walk on walls or ceilings. Reach would be assigned to advanced duration and you could activate in the same interval as Kinetic Efficiency. With that, you cover most acrobatics short of platforming on leaves and raindrops.</div> </div> </div> </div>The gravity control, bouncing off of leaves and such, sounds amazing, but I want to keep the third optional as it is, the original legacy in 1e allowed for the monks to throw punches at range and that feature is what made me want to work on this legacy. Maybe I'll give my monks an enchanted / imbued item to get the gravity effect, because that does sound amazing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481513-monks-perfected-adepts-2e-conversion?p=1481544#post1481544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fourth Life Attainment could be a variation of Shrink and Grow, allowing the mage to alter the size of any living being. Reach could be assigned to instant use and advanced duration. This allows them to have an even easier time staying close to enemies, gives them some extra Health (since Size affects that) and makes them far more difficult to target with spells. A master of Life would have a size of 5 (base) + 5 (Potency) + 2 (Legacy extra factor dice) = 12. This means all enemies need at least that to affect them or take extra time using something like Warding Gesture (which not everyone will have) or cast with AoE factors, which risks putting themselves and their allies in the crossfire. This way you avoid a functionality overlap between Mend and Knit, while also gaining an ability that is useful both in and out of combat (shrinking has a lot of creative stealth applications).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually great, definitely a change I'm going to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481513-monks-perfected-adepts-2e-conversion?p=1481544#post1481544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fourth optional Attainment is based on Flurry of Blows, correct ? In that case, utilizing a spell as a basis, I would say this is similar to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1053502#post1053502\">Gatling Assault</a>, with Reach used for instant use and medium burst autofire. It takes a turn to setup and van be used [Forces] times, but makes it unblockable if you can't defend against firearms.</div> </div> </div> </div>This attainment was made by someone else helping me, but now that you've said it I definitely see the FoB inspiration also<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481513-monks-perfected-adepts-2e-conversion?p=1481544#post1481544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The capstone Attainment can be used on both the monk or anyone they touch, by default spell rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>The theme I'm going for is mastery over your own body and anime fighter which is why I made limited this and the fourth attainment to casting on the monk but I wouldn't fault anyone for coming along and dismissing that limitation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481513-monks-perfected-adepts-2e-conversion?p=1481544#post1481544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last optional Attainment of Earthquake might be a bit too wide hitting for the self displine approach of the Legacy. An alternative could be to use Turn Momentum with Reach assigned to advanced duration, reflexive use and redirecting objects up to 90 degrees. This allows them to protect themselves plus cabalmates and control some of the chaos around them to their favor.<br /> <br /> Those would be my first thoughts on this conversion, the idea was to synergize the toolkit to create a highly mobile and versatile close range brawler. Hope it helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, anime theme here, the idea of splitting the ground from kinetic energy fits for me, but your suggestion is a good alternative for anyone who wants to move a little away from that basis. TYVM for the input here, lots of good changes to make when I'm back at my computer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}